----------
>2.      Is there any way of changing my process I.D. (as shown in the
>        dialogue in LPC) from the default of SYS$PRG0 to something relating
>        to my application. 

Msg #65 of 66   Time: 27 Sep 95  17:51:42
From: rburtonw@nyx10.cs.du.edu
To  : All
Subj: Process name change
---------[U.COMP.SYS.PSION]-----------------------------------------------
Author: Roger Burton-west   Address: rburtonw@nyx10.cs.du.edu

Here's a code fragment I threw together this morning. Just call it at
the beginning of the program with the process name you want to use (up
to 8 characters), which will then appear in the process table
(accessible via Spy and CMDP, among others) instead of the default
SYS$PRGO. This makes crashes much easier to resolve, and provides a
neater appearance.

Oh, in case anyone's wondering, this is so trivial (based on the
Psionics files, as usual) that I'm making it free for general use.

PROC callme:(v$)
  local pid%,k$(9),m%
  pid%=call($88)
  k$=v$+chr$(0)
  m%=addr(k$)+1
  call($c88,pid%,0,0,0,m%)
ENDP

Roger

